<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Lohara dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1003 CE – 1320 CE (approx.) · capital Srinagar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last major Hindu dynasty of Kashmir, under which Kalhana wrote his chronicle, the Rajatarangini.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1003 Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/didda">Didda</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/parvagupta-dynasty">Parvagupta dynasty</a> was succeeded by her nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangramaraja">Sangramaraja</a>, a prince of Lohara, a hill state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pir-panjal-range">Pir Panjal</a> range. He founded the Lohara dynasty and resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a>, whose attacks on the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lohkot">Lohkot</a> in 1015 and 1021 failed.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dynasty's reign was marked by struggles between kings and the landed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damaras">Damaras</a>. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha-of-kashmir">Harsha</a>, who ruled from 1089 to 1101, was a cultured patron but melted down temple images to pay his troops, and was killed in a revolt. A second branch began with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uchchala">Uchchala</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayasimha-of-kashmir">Jayasimha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalhana">Kalhana</a> wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajatarangini">Rajatarangini</a> in 1148 to 1149, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> verse history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> and one of the few true histories of early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Later Lohara kings were weak. After a Mongol raid under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulju">Dulucha</a> in 1320, the Ladakhi prince Rinchan seized power, and in 1339 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-mir">Shah Mir</a> founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kashmir-sultanate">Sultanate of Kashmir</a>, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> rule.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1003 CE – 1320 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.66%;width:6.31%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1003 CE – 1320 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Srinagar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sangramaraja, Harsha, Jayasimha</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Kashmiri</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a>, <a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Loharas of Kashmir</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1162&amp;focus=lohara-dynasty" aria-label="Lohara dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6585 942 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lohara dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6905 1198L6905 1198M6905 1198L6905 1198"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6905 1198h0M6905 1198h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6905 1198h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6905 1198h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Srinagar. <a href="/atlas?year=1162&amp;focus=lohara-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
